      "assumptions": [
        "Carrier Crash leaves all modeled variables unchanged and does not model durable flush or restart.",
        "Replay completion assumes scheduler fairness.",
        "The existing production property uses in-memory operation traces.",
        "D1 admission assumes valid samples, completing commands, and no external writes during the modeled decision.",
        "D2 probe admission assumes successful startup and completing probes, cleanup, and local writes.",
        "D2 sample validation abstracts numeric-prefix conversion and assumes completing commands, cleanup, and local writes.",
        "Emergency models assume completing record writes. Timeout models assume timer service and effective cancellation.",
        "The separate models do not establish a composed emergency deadline, confirmed termination, or durable publication.",
        "B16 assumes stable valid samples and completing local writes. Its production fixture covers only the low-space opening path.",
        "B17 assumes a completing guardian sample, local record, and stop request before benchmark return. It does not establish a composed deadline.",
        "B18 assumes effective command-group cancellation and completing local writes. Its eight-second fixture observation is not a complete production emergency deadline.",
        "B19 uses an atomic admission abstraction. The production liveness check and benchmark launch are not atomic.",
        "Progress models assume elapsed clock time and completing parent decisions. Atomic model transitions do not establish an atomic production admission or a complete deadline.",
        "B23 models cleanup client cancellation under effective signals and advancing abstract time. The production fixture checks refusal and local publication separately.",
        "B24 assumes signed 64-bit Bash arithmetic. Its finite model does not cover every input string or the two maximum-value production characterization cases.",
        "B25 disables age-only deletion. It does not establish a safe ownership protocol, space reclamation, Docker ownership, or a complete deadline.",
        "B26 assumes a sufficient final sample and summarizes pipeline outcomes sequentially. It does not prove pipeline timing, concurrent faults, or durable publication.",
        "B28 assumes successful writer termination before the abstract exit transition. The fixture checks termination after driver exit without measuring exact event ordering.",
        "B29 assumes a surviving state file, atomic record replacement, and one driver. Process-crash tests do not establish power-loss durability or concurrent recovery.",
        "B30 assumes authentic creation metadata in a cooperative Docker environment, successful selected termination, and no late creation.",
        "B31 assumes one uncommitted iteration and completing local record writes. It does not prove successful termination, atomic publication, or storage durability.",
        "Host ownership assumes stable cooperative metadata, same-user processes, and successful descriptor-based termination. Concurrent creation, hidden processes, and kernel faults remain open.",
        "The preference model assumes stable cooperative ownership and one atomic completing write. It does not guarantee kernel victim selection.",
        "B36 assumes successful cooperative creation without conflicting caller options. Atomic model transitions do not establish implementation atomicity or response deadlines.",
        "B37 assumes surviving uncorrupted storage and atomic recovery records. It does not establish power-loss durability or production crash-time writer termination."
      ],
      "bounds": [
        "Carrier: two signatures, three blocks, watermark zero, and scan start at most two.",
        "Replay: eight events, indexed replay, inline singleton, and yield interval four.",
        "Disk: initial free space 7000 MiB, floor 4096 MiB, band 4096 MiB, and samples 7000, 8191, 8192, 8193 MiB.",
        "D2 probe admission: valid samples 7000, 8192, and 16384 MiB, plus a separate missing sample at either probe.",
        "D2 sample validation: valid samples 7000, 8192, and 16384 MiB, plus a malformed field with numeric prefix 16384.",
        "Execution: two workers, 120-second configuration timeout, and 60-second kill grace.",
        "B7 through B12 have 5, 11, 4, 5, 129, and 6 distinct states in their corrected configurations.",
        "B13 has five distinct states. Abstract cancellation ticks do not establish a wall-clock emergency bound.",
        "B14 has four distinct states. Its atomic admission decision does not model a later crash or a live but stalled guardian.",
        "B15 has six distinct states. Its retained marker does not change during the opening benchmark decision.",
        "B16 has 12 distinct states. Samples are 7000, 8192, and 16384 MiB, with a 4096 MiB floor and band.",
        "B17 has five distinct states. Available space changes from 16384 to 1024 MiB, below the 2048 MiB hard floor.",
        "B18 has fourteen distinct states for guardian death and a disk breach. B19 reuses the four-state GuardianAdmission model and its exact control.",
        "B20 and B21 share the five-state GuardianProgress model and exact control. B22 has six states for fresh, equal-limit, and stale admission ages.",
        "B23 reuses the unchanged five-state DiskStopDeadline model with an explicit hygiene invariant alias.",
        "B24 has 88 distinct states for three exact invalid configurations and the valid default. Decimal column steps avoid native model-checker integer limits.",
        "B25 has four distinct states for an unowned session with a live writer and either an old or recent directory.",
        "B26 has 42 distinct states for five command outcomes with either one failure or no failure, followed by admission.",
        "B27, B28, and B29 have eight, four, and four distinct states. They cover three fixture resources, one successful writer stop, and two recovery attempts.",
        "B30 and B31 each have two distinct states. They model two existing Docker writers and one rejected exit stop, respectively.",
        "B32 and B33 use a two-state host ownership model. Their exact controls remove different observed writer sets.",
        "B34 has a two-state native preference model. The exact control also changes the unrelated node preference.",
        "B36 has three distinct states. Its exact control changes the unrelated container preference during a guardian sample.",
        "B37 has four distinct states for one benchmark crash and two recovery attempts."
      ],
